2. Diffusion times in the cell
Estimate the time \(t\sim L^2/(2D)\) it takes to diffuse a distance \(L\) for:

a protein (\(D\approx 10\) µm²/s) across a bacterium (1 µm) and across a eukaryotic cell (20 µm);
a neurotransmitter (\(D\approx 300\) µm²/s) across a synaptic cleft (20 nm);
the same protein along a 1 m long nerve axon.

What do the numbers tell you about where cells can rely on diffusion and where they need active transport?
